    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to bring to the market this fantastically presented and perfectly located terrace property in Leinster Terrace, Clondalkin, Dublin 22. Ideally located in the heart of Clondalkin Village, this well-positioned property benefits from an abundance of amenities right on its doorstep. The Mill Shopping Centre, a variety of local shops, cafés, pubs, restaurants, and schools are all within easy walking distance.\n\nCommuters will appreciate the excellent transport links, with convenient access to the N7, N4, and M50 motorway network, as well as a range of public transport services providing direct connections to and from Dublin City Centre.. Bright, spacious, and immaculately-presented accommodation of c. 86 Sq m can be found here and in brief comprises of entrance hall, lounge, open plan kitchen/diner, inner hall way utility access and shower room to the ground floor. upstairs was traditionally built as a 3 bed room but has been reconfigured over the years providing two large double bedrooms with the master benefitting from an ensuite. Externally to the rear you will find a low maintenance private rear garden and separate section providing a timber built shed and patio area. No.2 comes to the market in turn key condition having been meticulously maintained, improved and upgraded by its current owners. Further benefits here include triple glazed windows, gas central heating and heaps of character.\n\nDue to condition, spec and location we know this property will be extremely popular so please contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0860634889 or 014030720 to register your early interest.\n\nKey Features\nBER C1\nc. 86 Sqm\nCentrally located\nTriple glazed windows\nTurn key condition\nPrivate rear garden\nFull of character\nGas central heating\nHigh ceilings throughout\nImproved and upgraded\nWalking distance to all local amenities\nViewing highly advised\n\nDirections\nDriving through Clondalkin village on Tower Road towards The Mill Shopping Centre, take a left turn onto Old Nangor Road after you go past the Round Tower. Follow the road round and Leinster Terrace will be the first row of houses on your right hand side."
      },
      {
